<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Strike against BHP Steel called off.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Strike against BHP Steel called off.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unions involved in the metal trades industry said they have called off a planned strike at Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd (BHP) steelworks around Australia from Friday.</p>
<p>The one-day stoppage was aimed at securing a 15 percent wage rise over two years but the unions said a better-than-expected offer by BHP would now be discussed with the company on Friday.</p>
<p>BHP Steel has 20,000 union members.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
